    "body": "## Summary\n- Keep `.github/mergify.yml` unchanged: a new rule that drops the `#approved-reviews-by >= 1` condition would let a single leaked publish credential merge without any human review, so approval keeps coming from a separate identity instead.\n- Rework the identity/token design in `docs/i18n-community-translation-setup.md` §4 around two GitHub Apps (publish, approval): only their private keys and App IDs are stored long-term; installation tokens are minted fresh on every workflow run via `actions/create-github-app-token`. The `I18N_SYNC_PUBLISH_TOKEN`/`I18N_SYNC_APPROVAL_TOKEN` fixed-secret design is dropped.\n- Rewire `.github/workflows/i18n-sync-pull.yml` to mint both tokens at the start of the job, use the publish token for `actions/checkout`, and drop the `|| secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN` fallback so a missing App key fails loudly instead of silently producing a PR that can never pass `ci-app-lint` and clear the merge queue. Job `permissions` narrowed to `contents: read` since nothing writes with the workflow's own token anymore.\n- Record the mergify-vs-two-identities trade-off as a Decision in `research.md` so it isn't re-litigated, and rescope tasks 5.3/6.2 in `tasks.md` to the two-App design.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `git diff` reviewed; workflow YAML parsed successfully with `js-yaml` to confirm structure and step wiring\n- [x] Independent adversarial review (fresh Opus subagent) of the workflow diff against the setup doc, task text, and Requirements 3.3/3.4/8.1 — APPROVED, findings addressed (dropped leftover `GITHUB_TOKEN` env line, narrowed `permissions`, fixed a stale `_Blocked:_` note in tasks.md)\n- [ ] Task 4.2 (registering the two real GitHub Apps) remains blocked on a human with GROWI org GitHub permissions — this PR does not change that\n- [ ] Tasks 6.1/6.2 (real-environment verification) remain blocked on 4.2, unchanged\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CQDr55UMx8N93X1D8jUgRC",
